// The phone-only build settings: the one list both rolling phone builds use (#3354). scripts/phone-build (the Mac)
// and .github/workflows/phone-build.yml (GitHub-hosted, which the owner's Mac installs) each pass
// `-xcconfig Config/PhoneBuild.xcconfig`, so the two builds can't drift apart again: the hosted one dropped
// both settings until #3354. Both checks read the built app's Info.plist (SMPhoneBuild, SMShareLinkCreation)
// against this file before a build reaches the installer.
//
// Uploads never read this file. An upload is a plain Release archive (AGENTS.md "Releasing a build"), where
// project.yml sets both to NO; gates are set at build time, never switched on remotely (owner, 2026-10-17).
// scripts/tests/test_phone_build_gate.py fails if any other file passes these settings.
//
// SM_PHONE_BUILD turns on SM_PHONE_BUILD_CONDITIONS_YES in project.yml (the #3091 locked-Margin spike).
// SM_SHARE_LINK_CREATION turns on iPhone link creation (#487): the owner's 2026-11-02 call ships it to his own
// builds behind the build-time flag (docs/decisions.md).
SM_PHONE_BUILD = YES
SM_SHARE_LINK_CREATION = YES
